            {
              "id": "db5e8b03-c033-332f-b14d-c11d8a00f3e7",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "This finding is classified as a genuine vulnerability because the analysis identified a risk of undefined behavior due to possible overlap between the source and destination memory regions in the memory copy operation. The destination and source may refer to overlapping memory, as indicated by the dataflow analysis. Additionally, there is a risk that the source pointer could be null at runtime, as there is no prior check ensuring it is non-null. The destination is a pointer type, and there is no evidence that its capacity is being checked or that the copy length is derived from its size. No explicit null-termination or guard conditions are present. These factors together indicate a high likelihood of a real issue that could lead to memory corruption or program crashes.\n\n## In Context Remediation\nTo prevent undefined behavior when copying memory where the source and destination may overlap, use `memmove` instead of `memcpy`. `memmove` is designed to handle overlapping regions safely. Replace the original call with:\n\n```cpp\nmemmove(buf, addrInst, sizeof(addrInst));\n```\n\nAdditionally, ensure that both `buf` and `addrInst` are valid pointers and that the size argument does not exceed the capacity of the destination buffer. If there is any possibility that the source pointer could be null, add a check before the copy:\n\n```cpp\nif (addrInst != nullptr) {\n    memmove(buf, addrInst, sizeof(addrInst));\n}\n```\n\n## References\n- [CWE-119: Improper Restriction of Operations within the Bounds of a Memory Buffer](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/119.html)\n- [CWE-787: Out-of-bounds Write](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/787.html)\n- [OWASP Buffer Overflow](https://owasp.org/www-community/vulnerabilities/Buffer_Overflow)\n- [OWASP C-Based Toolchain Hardening Cheat Sheet](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/C-Based_Toolchain_Hardening_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n\n___\n"
              },
