              "id": "74ce3355-612e-311c-820d-381bc7f6e389",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "This finding is classified as a genuine vulnerability because the analysis identified a risk of undefined behavior due to possible overlap between the source and destination memory regions in the memory copy operation. The destination and source are both identifiers, and dataflow analysis suggests that the destination buffer may alias or overlap with the source. Additionally, there is no explicit check to ensure that the source pointer is not null, which increases the risk of a runtime error. The destination buffer is a pointer type, and there is no evidence that its capacity is being checked or that the copy length is derived from the destination's size. The absence of a guard or explicit null-termination further increases the risk. These factors indicate a high likelihood of a real issue that could lead to undefined behavior, memory corruption, or security vulnerabilities.\n\n## In Context Remediation\nTo prevent undefined behavior when copying memory, ensure that the source and destination buffers do not overlap. If there is any possibility of overlap, use `memmove` instead of `memcpy`, as `memmove` is designed to handle overlapping regions safely. Additionally, check that the source pointer is not null before performing the copy to avoid null pointer dereference.\n\n```cpp\nif (buf != nullptr && pltData != nullptr) {\n    memmove(buf, pltData, sizeof(pltData));\n}\n```\n\nIf you are certain that the buffers never overlap, document this assumption clearly in the code and consider adding runtime assertions to enforce it during development:\n\n```cpp\nassert(buf != pltData);\nmemcpy(buf, pltData, sizeof(pltData));\n```\n\n## References\n- [OWASP C-Based Toolchain Hardening Cheat Sheet](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/C-Based_Toolchain_Hardening_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n- [CWE-119: Improper Restriction of Operations within the Bounds of a Memory Buffer](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/119.html)\n- [CWE-787: Out-of-bounds 