            {
              "id": "3664a29a-2a56-35e9-a358-33a3d6eb4c73",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "This finding is classified as a genuine vulnerability because the analysis identified a risk of undefined behavior due to possible overlap between the source and destination memory regions in the memory copy operation. The destination and source expressions are related by data flow, which means they may refer to overlapping memory, and this is confirmed by the analysis. Additionally, there is no explicit check to ensure that the destination pointer is not null, which further increases the risk. The function does not include any guard to prevent this issue, and the classification explicitly states a risk of undefined behavior. These factors indicate that this is a real and actionable issue that should be addressed to prevent potential memory corruption or crashes.\n\n## In Context Remediation\nTo prevent undefined behavior when copying memory, ensure that the source and destination memory regions do not overlap. If there is any possibility of overlap, use a function that is safe for overlapping regions, such as `memmove`, instead of `memcpy`. Additionally, add checks to ensure that the destination pointer is not null before performing the copy operation.\n\n**Remediation example:**\n\n```cpp\nif (sym.Name.ShortName != nullptr && name.data() != nullptr) {\n    // Use memmove instead of memcpy if overlap is possible\n    memmove(sym.Name.ShortName, name.data(), name.size());\n}\n```\n\nThis change ensures that the copy operation is safe even if the source and destination regions overlap, and it also guards against null pointer dereference.\n\n## References\n- [OWASP C-Based Toolchain Hardening Cheat Sheet](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/C-Based_Toolchain_Hardening_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n- [CWE-119: Improper Restriction of Operations within the Bounds of a Memory Buffer](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/119.html)\n- [CWE-787: Out-of-bounds Write](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/787.html)\n- [OWASP Buffer Overflow](https://owasp.org/www-community/vulnerabilities/Buffer_Overflow)\n\n___\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "tags": [
                  "DS121708"
                ]
              }
